  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for letting us know. I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0101) and its main drive looks healthy right now: about 310 GB of 512 GB is free (around 60%), and the laptop isn't reporting any warnings. Before we go any further, could you help me with a few things? 1) Is the warning on this laptop, or on another computer? 2) Does it name a drive, such as D: or a USB or external drive? 3) Can you send a screenshot of the message, or tell me exactly what it says and when it last appeared? If you just want to free up some space anyway, you can empty the Recycle Bin and Downloads folder, then go to Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files and remove temporary files. Once I hear back, I'll take care of the rest.",
  "internal_note": "VIP user (CEO). Reported low disk space warning. lookup_user: one assigned device, BL-LT-0101. check_device_status: online, last check-in 2026-10-09 15:04 UTC, C: 512 GB total, 310 GB free (60.5%), no warnings. Per KB-017, under 10% is a problem, so the device data doesn't back up the report. Possible causes: a different machine, a secondary or external drive, an old notification, or a different message (e.g. OneDrive or mailbox storage; mailbox is only at 17.4%). Asked the user for the device, the drive letter, and a screenshot. Haven't made any changes. If a real low-space condition shows up and stays under 10% after cleanup, escalate per KB-017. Given VIP status, think about following up quickly.",
